The moon goes down, crows caw, frost fills the sky;
Maples by the river, fishing lamps face my sleepless grief.
Outside Gusu City, the Cold Mountain Temple;
Midnight bell tones reach the traveler's boat.

The moon sets, crows cry, frost fills the sky;  
By the river maples and fishing lights, I sorrowfully lie.  
Outside Gusu City stands Cold Mountain Temple;  
At midnight, its bell sounds reach the traveler's boat.
